al substrate because it is simpler, anti-scope-compliant, and reuses all existing WBC seams.\\\",\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"blocking_substrate_choice\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"question\\\": \\\"Can CL2 implementation proceed against the archived CL1 contract whose handoff has accepted_for_cl2: false? Per user direction, the planner proceeds with conservative repo-backed assumptions and lets critique/gate reject if needed. If this is unacceptable, all CL2 work blocks until the 5 procedural blockers resolve.\\\",\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"blocking_handoff_acceptance\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"assumptions\\\": [\\n    \\\"The real persistence substrate is the NDJSON append journal (arnold/runtime/event_journal.py) + pure fold (arnold/kernel/fold.py) + EffectEvidenceRecorder (arnold/kernel/effect_ledger.py). The brief's SQLite substrate does not exist and will not be built. This is a bridge: the brief's outcomes are preserved on the real substrate.\\\",\\n    \\\"CL2 implementation proceeds against the archived CL1 schema contracts (technically validated, all must-gates pass) despite the handoff being procedurally unaccepted (5 blockers). Every artifact encodes this assumption. Normal critique/gate/review phases can reject unsafe choices.\\\",\\n    \\\"All existing plan-local artifact paths remain writable during CL2 and become read-only projections after coordinated cutover in CL5. CL2 adds new domain events to the NDJSON journal, not to plan-local JSON files, so compatibility risk is low.\\\",\\n    \\\"Partially parseable attempts are admitted with ParseStatus indicating the recovery level (e.g., PARTIAL_RECOVERED) and an evidence_ref pointing to the recovered subset. Unparseable fields are stored as null with explicit unavailable_reason. Partial occurrences are evidence-only (cannot carry semantic_finding_id, cannot close a finding).\\\",\\n    \\\"All 5 cancelled CL2 artifacts are pre-amendment and none can be ported as-is. The archive is treated as read-on