(replay_result) producing the full cumulative/domain view.\\\",\\\"Write tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_replay.py: determinism (two replays produce byte-equivalent cumulative projection via JSON hash); no mutation (row counts unchanged); no external effect (no new rows in any write table); duplicate replay is a no-op.\\\"]},{\\\"step\\\":9,\\\"title\\\":\\\"Build active-action projection\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":3,\\\"actions\\\":[\\\"Add project_active_action(replay_result) to projections.py: three work queues must_act, must_revalidate, context_only. Open/findings needing revision \\u2192 must_act; stale/findings needing re-verification \\u2192 must_revalidate; closed/superseded/resolved \\u2192 context_only. Superseded decisions flagged (do not support clean gate projection). Batch actions enumerate every finding ID.\\\",\\\"Write tests in test_projections.py: bounds (closed history does not grow active set); queue routing; supersession (superseded in context_only not must_act); batch enumeration (every finding ID enumerable).\\\"]},{\\\"step\\\":10,\\\"title\\\":\\\"Build per-round accountability projection\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":3,\\\"actions\\\":[\\\"Add project_round_accountability(replay_result) to projections.py: maps full chain per round \\u2014 critic attempt \\u2192 occurrence \\u2192 logical finding/reconciliation \\u2192 response (declared) \\u2192 verified outcome (independent) \\u2192 reopen condition. Distinguishes reviser addressed claim from independently verified dealt_with|partially_dealt_with|not_dealt_with|unknown. Accounts for every parseable occurrence and active finding.\\\",\\\"Add round-receipt tests to test_projections.py: completeness (receipt maps every occurrence to a finding or legacy_unknown); chain integrity (response distinct from outcome); open findings accounted with current disposition and reopen condition.\\\"]}]},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Phase 5: Corrections, Audit, Tripwires, Freshness\\\",\\\"steps\\\":[{\\\"step\\\":11,\\\"title\\\":\\\"Supersession/correction replay and audit disagreement events\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":3,\\\"actions\\\":[\\\"Extend replay.py correction handling: when a reconciliation event has supersedes_event_id, replay derives the latest valid decision state (accepted|review_required|disputed|superseded) while retaining both original and superseding events in the cumulative projection.\\\",\\\"Extend audit handling: AuditEvent with audit_result=disputed marks the referenced finding as disputed; visible in active-action projection; cannot be silently overridden by closure.\\\",\\\"Write tests in test_replay.py / test_projections.py: correction supersession (both events present; latest state is superseding; gate flags it); audit disagreement (dispute event appended \\u2192 disputed visible; closure cannot silently preserve; actionable in must_revalidate).\\\"]},{\\\"step\\\":12,\\\"title\\\":\\\"Region-freshness vectors, deterministic tripwires, governed tombstone\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Large\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":4,\\\"actions\\\":[\\\"Create arnold/critique_ledger/freshness.py: region-anchor freshness (each finding declares stable section identity + content hashes; region change detection marks affected findings stale without full-ledger re-adjudication); scoped staleness (only findings whose region_anchors intersect changed region go stale); unknown/cross-cutting scope defaults to whole-plan freshness; region movement/split/merge becomes unresolved_mapping.\\\",\\\"Implement deterministic tripwires: fire on plan region change, evidence/dependency change, near-match, audit disagreement, stale model/schema revision. Trigger needs_reconciliation, never semantic merge/closure/suppression.\\\",\\\"Governed tombstone/unavailable handling: missing or redacted evidence surfaced as unknown in projections (not crashed, not suppressed, not leaked). Tombstone state visible.\\\",\\\"Write tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_freshness.py: region freshness (stales only affected findings); tripwire determinism (each trigger fires needs_reconciliation, never closure); tombstone (missing/redacted/unavailable surfaces as unknown; replay does not crash; tombstone visible); privacy (redacted evidence surfaced as unknown, never leaked).\\\"]}]},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Phase 6: One-Time Import\\\",\\\"steps\\\":[{\\\"step\\\":13,\\\"title\\\":\\\"Build legacy one-time importer\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":3,\\\"actions\\\":[\\\"Create arnold/critique_ledger/importer.py with LegacyImporter: reads retained legacy M6 artifacts (plan-local JSON); maps to v1 schemas via from_dict(mode='preserve'); classifies legacy semantic_finding_id as legacy_unknown; rejects unsupported target versions without partial publish; partially parseable attempts admitted with ParseStatus.PARTIAL_RECOVERED + evidence_ref + unavailable_reason; does not invent duplicate/resolution/evidence/reopen relationships; semantic gaps marked unknown.\\\",\\\"Write tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_importer.py: current-source (valid imports correctly); unsupported version (rejected, no partial publish); partial parse (admitted with PARTIAL_RECOVERED; gaps unknown); legacy semantic_finding_id (read compatibly, classified legacy_unknown).\\\"]},{\\\"step\\\":14,\\\"title\\\":\\\"Import fixture matrix\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":3,\\\"actions\\\":[\\\"Create tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_fixtures.py with parametrized fixture tests covering all 10 scenarios: current-source, target-only, future-version (rejected), corrupt (partial if recoverable), redacted (surfaced as unknown), unavailable (surfaced as unknown), duplicate (deduped), out-of-order (ordered by sequence), concurrent (serialized), crash (idempotent resume).\\\",\\\"Assert each fixture: correct admission/rejection, correct classification, no evidence invention, no partial publish of unsupported versions, no c