edgerMigrator` DDL migrations | Additive `schema_version` field on event envelopes + `cl.schema.v2` in `SUPPORTED_VERSIONS` |\\n| `SqliteLedgerOutbox` crash recovery | Journal IS the outbox \\u2014 `journal_cursor()` + `detect_journal_drift()` prove custody |\\n| `payload_policy.py` reuse | `EffectEvidenceRecorder` Protocol reuse (`arnold/kernel/effect_ledger.py`) |\\n| SQLite domain tables + 6 indexes | Critique event kinds appended to journal; `fold_journal(events, kind_filter, projector, initial)` sorts by seq |\\n\\n**Resolution: this is a BRIDGE, not a contradiction.** The brief's OUTCOME and DONE-CRITERIA are sound. Only the implementation substrate is wrong, and the real substrate is simpler, anti-scope-compliant (no new DB service), and reuses every existing WBC seam.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Summary of Steps\\n\\n| Phase | Steps | What |\\n|-------|-------|------|\\n| 1. Foundation | 1\\u20133 | Port CL1 schemas/loop from archive; add v2 versioning (deprecate `semantic_finding_id` on occurrences, add `supersedes_event_id`/`region_anchors`/`tripwire_state`, new `FindingResponseEvent`/`OutcomeVerificationEvent`/`AuditEvent`) |\\n| 2. Journal layer | 4\\u20135 | `CritiqueLedgerWriter` with batch-atomic flock append + idempotency dedup; `EffectEvidenceRecorder` adapter |\\n| 3. Projections | 6\\u20138 | Cumulative/domain fold + read-only replay orchestrator; bounded active-action projection (must_act/must_revalidate/context_only); per-round accountability chain |\\n| 4. Amendment | 9\\u201311 | Correction/supersession replay; region-freshness vectors + deterministic tripwires; audit disagreement + governed tombstone |\\n| 5. Import + audit | 12\\u201313 | One-time legacy importer (10 fixture types); cancelled CL2 archive audit (SHA-256 hashes, non-adoption boundary) |\\n| 6. Validation | 14\\u201315 | 8 test files (schema golden, atomicity, replay, projections, freshness, import, negative-mutation, concurrency); handoff JSON + compatibility |\\n\\n---\\n\\n```json\\n{\