,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":5,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"Defines a new schema state-machine (versioned, checksum-validated, forward-fix-only migrations the migrator enforces) whose columns must exactly match the v2 dataclasses; an idempotency or checksum mistake silently corrupts crash-resume, earning tier 5.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T5\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Build the domain append layer with atomic occurrence+manifest+outbox commit in one BEGIN IMMEDIATE\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Create arnold/critique_ledger/store.py with a CL2 domain store that shares the SQLite WAL connection with SqliteAttemptLedgerStore (same DB, separate class \\u2014 not a subclass, not a parallel authority). append_occurrence() writes occurrence + LedgerRevisionManifest + outbox entry atomically inside a single BEGIN IMMEDIATE via SqliteLedgerOutbox.append_event_with_outbox on the shared connection, so a simulated mid-tx crash leaves no partial accepted ledger revision. Enforce idempotency-key dedup (no double-insert), quarantine divergent duplicates, and single-terminal enforcement. Reuse (do not reimplement) the WBC substrate's WAL/isolation_level=None/busy-retry/_append_tx primitives and payload_policy InlinePayloadPolicy for inline/retention/redaction. Partial occurrences are evidence-only (ParseStatus.PARTIAL_RECOVERED, cannot carry semantic_finding_id, cannot close \\u2014 SD4). Add tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_store_append.py: atomic commit, mid-tx-crash leaves no partial state, idempotency dedup, divergent-duplicate quarantine, partial-publication cannot expose incomplete revision. Run store append tests.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":15,\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"T2\\\",\\\"T4\\\"],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{\\\"T2\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The store serializes v2 schema records into domain tables and must enforce PARTIAL_RECOVERED evidence-only semantics\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"schemas.py v2 dataclasses + 