\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":4,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"Verbatim copy of 3 self-contained files is mechanical, but it establishes the module contract every downstream task depends on and the golden round-trip test must catch any silent copy/import error; a dropped export or wrong SCHEMA_VERSION constant cascades into all later tasks.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T2\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Add additive v2 schema versioning to schemas.py preserving v1 deserialization\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Extend schemas.py additively: add SCHEMA_VERSION_V2='cl.schema.v2' and CompatibilityProfile.V2_STRICT alongside the existing v1 constants (do not remove/rename v1). Add v2-only fields with defaults so v1 records still deserialize: supersedes_event_id (Optional[str]), region_anchors (tuple), tripwire_state (mapping) on the occurrence/reconciliation envelopes. Add new response/outcome/audit event dataclasses (RevisionResponseEvent, VerifiedOutcomeEvent, AuditDisagreementEvent, SupersedesReconciliationEvent) with to_dict/from_dict and canonical_hash. Enforce that v2 strict-mode occurrences REJECT semantic_finding_id on raw occurrences (raw occurrences never author semantic identity \\u2014 North Star invariant 16) while v1_preserve still accepts legacy records. Extend test_schemas_golden.py: v2 round-trip, v1-records-still-deserialize under v2 reader, strict-mode rejection assertion. Run the golden suite.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":15,\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"T1\\\"],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{\\\"T1\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"v2 additions are layered onto the ported schemas.py and must not regress the v1 golden round-trip T1 established\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/schemas.py ported from CL1 + passing test_schemas_golden.py\\\"}},\\\"routing_group\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"write_set\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/schemas.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_schemas_golden.py\\\"],\\\"complete\\\":true},\\\"narrow_tests\\\":{\\\"selectors\\\":[\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_schemas_golden.py\\\"],\\\"max_seconds\\\":120,\\\"max_runs\\\":2},\\\"checkpoint\\\":{\\\"required\\\":false,\\\"max_interval_seconds\\\":300,\\\"records\\\":[]},\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"executor_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":6,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"Changes the schema contract the entire ledger depends on: new version constant, strict-mode rejection semantics, and four new event dataclasses with backward-compatible defaults that must keep v1 records deserializing \\u2014 a subtle field-default or strict-mode error passes simple tests but corrupts reconciliation, so it earns tier 6 not lower.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T3\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Make the pure semantic_loop functions v2-aware without changing v1 behavior\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Update semantic_loop.py pure functions (apply_disposition_events, apply_reconciliation_events, build_briefing, construct_manifest, project_gate_input, project_reviser_input, replay_full, validate_occurrence_custody) to accept and propagate v2 fields (supersedes_event_id, region_anchors, tripwire_state) and the new response/outcome/audit/supersedes event types. Superseded reconciliation events must yield latest accepted decision state while retaining both original and superseding events (North Star invariant 5/15). Add tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_semantic_loop.py: replay over a supersession chain resolves to the latest accepted decision; tripwire_state propagates into briefing/projection outputs; v1-only inputs still produce identical outputs to the ported v1 behavior. Run the semantic loop tests.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":12,\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"T1\\\",\\\"T2\\\"],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{\\\"T1\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The loop functions live in the ported semantic_loop.py and must be extended in place\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/semantic_loop.py ported from CL1\\\"},\\\"T2\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The loop must handle the v2 fields and new event dataclasses T2 defines\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"schemas.py v2 dataclasses (supersedes_event_id, region_anchors, tripwire_state, response/outcome/audit events)\\\"}},\\\"routing_group\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"write_set\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/semantic_loop.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_semantic_loop.py\\\"],\\\"complete\\\":true},\\\"narrow_tests\\\":{\\\"selectors\\\":[\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_semantic_loop.py\\\"],\\\"max_seconds\\\":120,\\\"max_runs\\\":2},\\\"checkpoint\\\":{\\\"required\\\":false,\\\"max_interval_seconds\\\":300,\\\"records\\\":[]},\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"executor_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":5,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"Extends already-pure deterministic functions to thread v2 fields through reconciliation/briefing/projection and resolve supersession to latest-accepted state; the logic is well-understood but the supersession-resolution and tripwire-propagation paths are non-obvious enough to need deliberate care, placing it at tier 5.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T4\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Define CL2 domain DDL migrations as forward-fix-only registry versions 5+\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Create arnold/critique_ledger/cl2_migrations.py defining domain table DDL as Migration(version=5+...) entries with idempotent statements (CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS) for the cumulative occurrence, reconciliation-event, disposition-event, response/outcome/audit-event, manifest, and tripwire tables whose columns mirror the v2 schema fields. Add a combined-registry helper, e.g. default_cl2_migrations() returning default_m6a_migrations()+CL2_tuple (NOTE: the plan assumption names default_combined_migrations() which does not exist \\u2014 build the combination here; do NOT edit arnold/workflow/ledger_migrations.py per SD2). Verify SqliteLedgerMigrator(store, registry) applies versions 5+ idempotently, is crash-resume safe, and that editing an applied migration's statements raises MigrationChecksumMismatchError. Add tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_cl2_migrations.py. Run the migration tests.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":13,\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"T2\\\"],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{\\\"T2\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The DDL column set must mirror the v2 schema fields (supersedes_event_id, region_anchors, tripwire_state, response/outcome/audit events) T2 defines so stored rows round-trip\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"schemas.py v2 dataclass field set\\\"}},\\\"routing_group\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"write_set\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/cl2_migrations.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_cl2_migrations.py\\\"],\\\"complete\\\":true},\\\"narrow_tests\\\":{\\\"selectors\\\":[\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_cl2_migrations.py\\\"],\\\"max_seconds\\\":120,\\\"max_runs\\\":2},\\\"checkpoint\\\":{\\\"required\\\":false,\\\"max_interval_seconds\\\":300,\\\"records\\\":[]},\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"executor_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":5,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"Defines a new schema state-machine (versioned, checksum-validated, forward-fix-only migrations the migrator enforces) whose columns must exactly match the v2 dataclasses; an idempotency or checksum mistake silently corrupts crash-resume, earning tier 5.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T5\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Build the domain append layer with atomic occurrence+manifest+outbox commit in one BEGIN IMMEDIATE\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Create arnold/critique_ledger/store.py with a CL2 domain store that shares the SQLite WAL connection with Sqlite