},\\\"checkpoint\\\":{\\\"required\\\":true,\\\"max_interval_seconds\\\":300,\\\"records\\\":[\\\"completed_subobjectives\\\",\\\"remaining_subobjectives\\\",\\\"output_hashes\\\",\\\"test_state\\\"]},\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"executor_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":8,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"Major subsystem with genuine concurrency/transaction-semantics risk: atomic cross-table append on a shared WAL connection, idempotency-key dedup, single-terminal enforcement, divergent-duplicate quarantine, and outbox integration where a mid-tx-crash or dedup error silently corrupts ledger integrity \\u2014 mistakes here pass simple tests but break under contention, placing it at tier 8.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T6\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Build the read-only deterministic cumulative/domain projection and replay engine\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Create arnold/critique_ledger/replay.py as a pure read-only module that reconstructs the cumulative finding set and per-domain projections by replaying stored events through the v2-aware semantic_loop functions. Replay must be deterministic (same inputs -> byte-identical cumulative projection across runs) and provably side-effect-free: no model call, no mutation, no external effect, no write to plan/gate/lifecycle/queue. It reads only committed rows and derives semantic finding identity, dispositions, and supersession (latest-accepted state while retaining both events). Add tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_replay.py: deterministic replay of a fixture event stream produces byte-identical output across two runs, read-only assertion (no store/gate/queue mutation), and supersession resolves to latest accepted. Run replay tests.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":15,\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"T3\\\",\\\"T5\\\"],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{\\\"T3\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Replay drives stored events through the v2-aware semantic_loop functions T3 extended\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"semantic_loop.py v2-aware replay_full/apply_* functions\\\"},\\\"T5\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Replay reads the committed occurrence/manifest/event rows the store appends\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"store.py committed append interface + row schema\\\"}},\\\"routing_group\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"write_set\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/replay.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_replay.py\\\"],\\\"complete\\\":true},\\\"narrow_tests\\\":{\\\"selectors\\\":[\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_replay.py\\\"],\\\"max_seconds\\\":120,\\\"max_runs\\\":2},\\\"checkpoint\\\":{\\\"required\\\":true,\\\"max_interval_seconds\\\":300,\\\"records\\\":[\\\"completed_subobjectives\\\",\\\"remaining_subobjectives\\\",\\\"output_hashes\\\",\\\"test_state\\\"]},\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"executor_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":7,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"Demanding deterministic-engine work over a broad surface: byte-identical replay across runs, provable read-only/no-mutation guarantees, and correct supersession-to-latest-accepted resolution \\u2014 a non-determinism or side-effect bug is subtle and passes naive tests, earning tier 7.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T7\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Build the bounded active-action projection (must_act | must_revalidate | context_only)\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Extend arnold/critique_ledger/projections.py (create it) with the active-action projection derived from T6 replay output. Expose must_act | must_revalidate | context_only per finding. Enforce: closed history does not grow must_act (active set stays bounded as history grows), unaudited non-action cannot remove a finding from the active set (North Star invariant 10), and batch actions enumerate every finding ID. Add active-action tests to tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_projections.py: closed finding moves out of must_act, unaudited non-action leaves it in, batch action covers all IDs, projection bounded as closed history grows. Run projection tests.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":13,\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"T6\\\"],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{\\\"T6\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The active-action projection is derived from the cumulative replay output T6 produces\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"replay.py cumulative projection interface\\\"}},\\\"routing_group\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"write_set\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/projections.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_projections.py\\\"],\\\"complete\\\":true},\\\"narrow_tests\\\":{\\\"selectors\\\":[\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_projections.py\\\"],\\\"max_seconds\\\":120,\\\"max_runs\\\":2},\\\"checkpoint\\\":{\\\"required\\\":false,\\\"max_interval_seconds\\\":300,\\\"records\\\":[]},\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"executor_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":6,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"The must_act/must_revalidate/context_only classification plus the load-bearing invariant that unaudited non-action cannot remove a finding is the gate's authority boundary \\u2014 a wrong classification silently lets closure slip through, so tier 6.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T8\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Build the per-round accountability receipt projection\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Extend arnold/critique_ledger/projections.py with the per-round accountability projection mapping the full chain attempt -> occurrence -> finding -> response -> verified outcome -> reopen for every parseable occurrence and active finding. Reviser 'addressed' must be distinct from independently-verified outcome. Every parseable occurrence and active finding must be accounted for (no silent omission). Add per-round-accountability tests to tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_projections.py: receipt covers all occurrenc